## sess111 — blocker 6 audited, measured, and my fix rejected by the ruling

**The audit.** `caw_drop_own_waiter` (`dlm/dlm_caw.c:2318`) clears `waiters`/`waiters_ex`/`holders[giveup_mode]` keyed on `ctx->node_bit` alone, from three post-giveup call sites. The adopt arm (`dlm_caw.c:2823`) writes **nothing** — pure recognition. So the on-disk image is *identical* for "handoff landed, nobody adopted" and "handoff landed and another local thread adopted it and is live": node identity is one bit and adoption leaves no trace. The ruling's "compare epoch/generation + holder mode" **cannot be satisfied from the slot**. Same-node concurrency is real by design — the `ISTATE_ACQUIRING` park exempts the demoter (`xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:28141`, `:28415`), and the tree already labels `P3A-DEMOTER-SLOWACQ` in-source as "the prime suspect for the same-node concurrent-request collision".

**The measurement** (32/caw on 0.11.440, `tests/census_p.sh`, 27/32 reporting): `P3A-DEMOTER-SLOWACQ`, `P6H-ABORT-RECONCILE`, acquire-timeout, `P-CAWEXH`, `P91-CLAIMEXH` — **all 0 on every node**, against ~970 adopts/node. The reconcile arm is never entered under a healthy board. Reachable by construction, unobserved in practice; RULE 6 forbids closing on that.

**The RULE-5 ruling rejected my fix** (`ctx->held` + a `modes[]` guard): it leaves an observe-to-track window, and — the part I had not seen — *multiple local attempts share one on-disk bit*, so one attempt's cancel destroys another's request whether or not a holder is involved. A generation-bumping adopt CAS is also insufficient (generation moves for unrelated reasons). Required instead: one authoritative per-(node,resource) local state machine, at most one on-disk request per node per resource with local callers joining it, adopt and reconcile serialized through slot validation, and fence-before-purge — the certificate must gate the **grant purge**, not only the recovery publish, because "lease expiry is a failure detector, not a fence."

**Three new defects filed** (`./defects.sh`, ledger now 28 open of 67, 16 critical):
- `D-SAMENODE-WAITER-CANCEL-COLLISION` (critical) — one bit per node cannot represent two local requests
- `D-RECONCILE-EXHAUSTION-SILENT` (high) — 1000 failed CAS attempts then a `void` return into normal service, on the path whose leak already caused a measured 16-node reader-starvation wedge
- `D-TRACK-PUBLISH-ORDERING` (high) — `ctx->held` is telemetry being used as synchronization, with a sticky overflow latch

Full ruling and the next session's start point are in ccmemory `ccloop-c7ee71c6-sess111-GPT-ruling-blocker6-REJECTS-held-table-guard`: build the per-resource registry in `dlm/dlm_caw.c`, modelled on the `ctx->grant_meta` cache, with attempts joining by refcount so cancel fires only as the last one out.

**Criteria: NO — not production ready.** 28 open defects, 16 critical. This session closed no ledger entry and opened three; the marker stays unwritten.

